cache
__pycache__
.venv
.vscode/
# Local secrets (MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN, PS_INTERNAL_API_KEY) — never commit.
.env
*.jsonl
*.submitted
nohup.out
smoke_check

# Run directories: track only the small, high-value files (provenance + hand-labeled
# verdicts); results and resume caches stay local.
runs/**
!runs/*/
!runs/*/manifest.json
!runs/*/area.geojson
!runs/*/*_verdicts.json
!runs/*/*.submission.json
# Position check (position_check.py, run by main.py at the end of every run): the verdict
# and its self-contained report stay with the run's provenance — including the
# <stem>.position_check.json written beside a repositioned submission, since its
# *.submission.json is tracked and the verdict it shipped under must be too. The
# reposition output itself and the Overpass cache beside them are not.
!runs/*/position_check.json
!runs/*/position_report.html
!runs/*/*.position_check.json
!runs/*/*.position_report.html
# Server-side clustering evaluation (scripts/eval_ps_clustering.py, protocol and
# findings in docs/ps-clustering-eval.md): the report and its per-arm CSV are the
# study's evidence, small and stable, so they are tracked like manifest.json. The
# two API pulls they are computed from are NOT — tens of MB apiece — so the report
# carries each one's url, fetch time, sha256 and feature count instead.
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/report.md
!runs/*/ps_clustering_eval*/arms.csv
# Camera-rig labels already live on a server (detectors.on_camera_rig; see the nadir-mask
# section of CLAUDE.md). These are the evidence base for the mask AND the exact set a
# cleanup would retire, so they have to outlive both the database state and the API pull
# they were derived from — the file records that pull's url and sha256 for the tie-back.
!runs/*/rig_labels.json
# Per-rig camera heights for Mapillary runs (scripts/mapillary_height.py, issue #53): the
# table `fuse_sites.py --camera-height-m per-rig` reads, bound to results.jsonl by sha256.
!runs/*/camera_heights.json
# The #87 height-gap study (scripts/height_gap.py; docs/mapillary-camera-height.md section 7):
# its CSVs and report are the evidence and are tracked. camera_height/groups.csv stays local.
!runs/*/camera_height/
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/*.csv
!runs/*/camera_height/gap/report.md
# AI-vs-crowd agree rate (scripts/agree_rate.py, write-up in docs/agree-rate-<city>.md): the
# report and CSVs are the evidence and are tracked. The three API pulls they are computed
# from (the frozen crowd snapshot) are NOT — the report carries each one's url, fetch time,
# sha256 and feature count instead.
!runs/*/agree_rate/
!runs/*/agree_rate/report.md
!runs/*/agree_rate/*.csv
# DEM road grade (scripts/dem_grade.py, #51; write-up in docs/dem-grade-study.md): the tile
# manifest (service, request, per-tile sha256) and the agreement report are tracked. The
# tiles themselves (tens to hundreds of MB) and grades.csv are NOT — the report carries
# grades.csv's sha256, and tiles.json is enough to refetch and verify every tile.
!runs/*/dem/
!runs/*/dem/tiles.json
!runs/*/dem/report.md
# Per-pano camera-height QC tests (scripts/height_qc.py, issue #44; write-up in
# docs/camera-height-study.md): the pre-registered verdicts and their tables are tracked.
# runs/_pooled/height_qc/ holds the cross-city verdicts the rule in depth.py follows.
!runs/*/height_qc/
!runs/*/height_qc/report.md
!runs/*/height_qc/*.csv
